From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 19:26:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: dma: apple,sio: let the boot loader enable the
 T8132 SIO

The T8132 SIO node had to stay disabled because no boot loader built its
firmware tables, and it was the only SIO without dma-channels.

m1n1 now builds the T8132's tables in the protocol-10 layout and enables
the node through its "sio" alias, as for the T6030. Drop the disabled
requirement and require dma-channels on every SIO; the T8132 keeps its
second (auxiliary) register window.

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5.5
---
 .../devicetree/bindings/dma/apple,sio.yaml          | 13 +++----------
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 10 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/dma/apple,sio.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/dma/apple,sio.yaml
index 5ac7c88cd4..a53ffb9fb6 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/dma/apple,sio.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/dma/apple,sio.yaml
@@ -10,8 +10,8 @@ description:
   SIO is a coprocessor on Apple M1 and later chips (and maybe also on earlier
   chips). Its role is to offload SPI, UART and DisplayPort audio transfers,
   being a pretend DMA controller.
-  The T8132 resource description remains disabled until its channel layout
-  and firmware handoff are supported; its channel count is not guessed.
+  On the T8132 the boot loader builds the firmware tables and enables the
+  node; the node describes an auxiliary register window as well.
 
 maintainers:
   - Martin Povišer <povik+lin@cutebit.org>
@@ -30,16 +30,10 @@ allOf:
         reg:
           minItems: 2
           maxItems: 2
-        status:
-          const: disabled
-      required:
-        - status
     else:
       properties:
         reg:
           maxItems: 1
-      required:
-        - dma-channels
 
 properties:
   compatible:
@@ -57,8 +51,6 @@ properties:
     description:
       Coprocessor register window, followed by an auxiliary window on T8132.
 
-  status: true
-
   '#dma-cells':
     const: 1
     description:
@@ -117,6 +109,7 @@ required:
   - compatible
   - reg
   - '#dma-cells'
+  - dma-channels
   - mboxes
   - iommus
   - power-domains
